- /projects/dash-mobile-render-20260930/NOTES.md  (appended "Step 3 — real payloads recorded")
- recorder: /projects/dash-mobile-render-20260930/tools/capture/record.mjs + probe.mjs

NUMBERS
- sessions in GET /api/sessions: 102 (envelope {"success":true,"data":[…]} — NOT a bare array; 43 distinct keys)
- websocket frames recorded: 945 across 6 files (primary 25 s file: 522)
- events captured: 8435 (live `event` frames + inner objects of `event_replay`)
- distinct eventType values: 17
- distinct non-event frame types: 21

HOW (from host:dash-mobile-render-20260930-worker, node v22 + curl, no browser)
  curl -s http://100.65.131.102:8000/api/sessions -o …/fixtures/sessions.json
  curl -s -X POST http://100.65.131.102:8000/api/ws-ticket -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"scope":"browser"}'
    -> {"success":true,"data":{"ticket":"77RMNnQZgIJVUXex4YKcwffPMDoSZB7Xe2QLKXl1EKA"}}
  node record.mjs <out.jsonl> <sessionId> <seconds>   # fresh ticket per connect (single-use),
    ws://100.65.131.102:8000/ws?ticket=<t>, send {"type":"subscribe","sessionId":"<id>","lastSeq":0},
    append every frame verbatim, one JSON per line.

THE 17 event.data KEY SETS (verbatim)
  message_start: {message, nonce, type}
  message_update: {assistantMessageEvent, message, type}
  message_end: {entryId, message, nonce, type}
  tool_call: {input, toolCallId, toolName, type}
  tool_execution_start: {args, toolCallId, toolName, type}
  tool_execution_update: {args, partialResult, toolCallId, toolName, type}
  tool_result: {content, details, input, isError, toolCallId, toolName, type}
  tool_execution_end: {__truncated, details, eventType, isError, reason, result, thresholdBytes, toolCallId, toolName, type}
  turn_start: {timestamp, turnIndex, type}
  turn_end: {contextUsage, message, toolResults, turnIndex, type}
  stats_update: {contextUsage, cost, tokensIn, tokensOut, turnUsage}
  custom_entry: {customType, data, entryId, groupId, type}
  agent_start: {type}
  before_agent_start: {prompt, systemPrompt, systemPromptOptions, type}
  agent_end: {__truncated, eventType, messages, reason, thresholdBytes, type}
  model_select: {model, type}
  resources_discover: {cwd, reason, type}
Counts: message_update 4805, message_end 791, message_start 763, custom_entry 257, turn_start 254,
tool_execution_start 253, tool_call 253, tool_result 250, tool_execution_end 250, turn_end 250,
stats_update 250, tool_execution_update 20, agent_start 13, agent_end 9, before_agent_start 9,
model_select 4, resources_discover 4.

THE [object Object] SOURCES (every one is an OBJECT or ARRAY in the live data)
- envelope nests twice: {type:"event", seq, sessionId, event:{eventType, timestamp, data:{…}}}; event_replay wraps the same object again as {events:[{seq, event:{…}}]}. Code that reads msg.data sees undefined.
- data.message is an object; data.message.content is an ARRAY of part objects. Part types seen: thinking (9764), toolCall (1335), text (1057). A toolCall part is {"type":"toolCall","id":"…","name":"ipython","arguments":{"code":"…"}} — arguments is an object.
- message.usage.cost is an object of 5 numbers, not a number.
- message_end for role "custom" has message.content as a PLAIN STRING (customType "goal_context"); roles assistant/toolResult use the array form. One code path cannot render both.
- turn_end.toolResults is an ARRAY of toolResult messages, each with its own content array and details object.
- tool_result.content ARRAY of {"type":"text","text":"…"}. tool_execution_end.result is an OBJECT usually, but a STRING in some frames, and a truncation marker ({__truncated, reason, thresholdBytes}) when over the cap.
- stats_update.turnUsage and .contextUsage are objects. custom_entry.data is the goal object (customType thread_goal_state; ALL 257 custom_entry events are that type). model_select.model is an object. before_agent_start.systemPromptOptions is an object.
- /api/sessions object/array fields: autoNamerState, notifyLog, pendingQueues, processMetrics, processes, uiModules. Everything else is string/number/boolean/null (currentTool is null in 76 of 102).

ONE THING TO KNOW: artifacts/fixtures/ws-01a0e8a9-17a0.jsonl appeared in the directory during my run and is NOT mine (name is not a session UUID). I left it untouched and excluded it from every count; checks/10-fixtures-valid.sh skips it. Worth knowing in case it is a truncated filename from another worker.

